  "description": "The reusable phasor-model engine from PrismFormer: define a model, train it data-parallel through an EvalApp pipeline, and run inference (predict / generate, with an optional KV cache). Ships two param-for-param comparable cores â€” AlgFormer (softmax dot-product attention) and HoloFormer (holographic-native attention: bind the key to its value, causally bundle into one superposed memory trace, then resonate the query to retrieve, O(TÂ·d) with O(1) KV-serve) â€” plus HoloShape capacity-law sizing, compute-equivalent (invisible-param) accounting, a built-in subword tokenizer, checkpoint save/load with in-place growth (context/shifts/vocabulary), and MQTT-based distributed/swarm training. HoloFormer also ships an opt-in, default-OFF per-layer Adam gate (\"ADAM & EVE\") that nudges a layer's update toward a codebook-derived target norm range; it is new, has not yet run a real training step, and does nothing unless explicitly enabled. Pure double[] + SIMD, no external ML runtime. Built on the Phasor VSA codec and the EvalApp pipeline runtime.",
